            "retrieved": null
          },
          "quote": "Mutants were scored as correct if two or more colonies had the expected structure based on PCR tests for both junction fragments.",
          "note": "the minimum verified colonies for an obtained deletion; applied to Table 3's '5. verified' column it reproduces 3,985 / 303 and Table 6 exactly"
        },
        {
          "value": "candidates for essential genes",
          "provenance": {
            "source_uri": "paper/PMC1681482.1.txt",
            "citation_key": "babaConstructionEscherichiaColi2006",
            "sha256": "6e39bc2f12aecceac568f91dfcd068e109433132df618dc68624d317737bf3cd",
            "method": "PMC Article Datasets plain text of the article (raw mirror)",
            "page": null,
            "retrieved": null
          },
          "quote": "Based on finding mutants with the predicted structure, these 3985 genes are (probably) nonessential, while the 303 genes (including 37 genes of unknown function), for which no mutants were found, are candidates for essential genes",
          "note": "what is_essential=True means here: a candidate, from a construction that yielded no mutant with the expected structure (#924)"
        },
        {
          "value": "a recovery method does not call a slow grower essential",
          "provenance": {
            "source_uri": "paper/PMC1681482.1.txt",
            "citation_key": "babaConstructionEscherichiaColi2006",
            "sha256": "6e39bc2f12aecceac568f91dfcd068e109433132df618dc68624d317737bf3cd",
            "method": "PMC Article Datasets plain text of the article (raw mirror)",
            "page": null,
            "retrieved": null
          },
          "quote": "Because genetic footprinting measures cell populations, a mutation causing slow growth can lead to under-representation of the mutant and hence false classification of many genes as essential. In contrast, we sought deletion mutants as survivors without regard to growth rate.",
          "note": "the paper's own statement of how its evidence differs from a population method's; carried on every record's evidence (#924)"
        }
      ],
